# Blinkwatch environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local overrides. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# The Blinkwatch project currently does not require external credentials or
# custom application variables. This file documents the expected format when
# real configuration is introduced alongside the feature that needs it.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public variables (browser-exposed)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are available in Client Components.
# The prefix means the value is intentionally public and must never hold secrets.
# Public values are embedded during `next build`; changing them after a production
# build may not update an already generated client bundle.
#
# Example (fictional — not used by the project today):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAMPLE_URL=https://example.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only variables (never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for secrets)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Server-only values belong in modules under `src/shared/config/env/server.ts`.
# Secrets, API keys, and private tokens must never use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# NODE_ENV is set automatically by Node.js and Next.js (development, test, or
# production). You normally should not configure it manually in `.env.local`.
